  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Kyra Vrisi.</p>\r\n<div>\u00a0</div>\r\n<div>Information about recent excavations, including preliminary field reports through the 2007 dig season, may be found on the website of the <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"http://isthmia.osu.edu/\">Ohio State University Excavations at Isthmia</a>. The American School of Classical Studies in Athens publishes the <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"http://www.ascsa.edu.gr/index.php/publications/browse-by-series/isthmia\">official, final reports in the series \"Isthmia.\"</a>\u00a0</div>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Isthmia was a major sanctuary located on the Isthmus of Corinth, which was sacred to Poseidon and Melikertes Palaimon, and site of the panhellenic Isthmian games.",
